title: FarField
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Guijia
    website: https://123zgj123.github.io
repository-code: https://github.com/123zgj123/FarField
url: https://github.com/123zgj123/FarField
abstract: >-
  FarField is a local research loop for automated scientific inquiry.
  Given a topic, it recovers development trajectories from verified
  papers and makes far-field jumps, proposes a falsifiable hypothesis,
  registers a two-arm experiment before any result is observed, and
  emits a protocol another researcher can rerun. Binding,
  construction, lever, and probe must be the same scientific object.
  The model proposes claims and scripts; graph checks, prior-art checks,
  world binding, and two-arm arithmetic are ordinary Python. Synthetic
  or generated data may weaken a claim and cannot corroborate it.
keywords:
  - scientific discovery
  - automated research
  - reproducibility
  - hypothesis testing
  - experimental design
  - evidence
  - research protocol
